---
id: no-rest-destructuring
title: Disallow object rest destructuring on query results
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use object rest destructuring on query results automatically subscribes to every field of the query result, which may cause unnecessary re-renders.\nThis makes sure that you only subscribe to the fields that you actually need."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rule-details","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rule Details"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"incorrect"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/no-rest-destructuring\": \"warn\" */\n\nconst useTodos = () => {\n  const { data: todos, ...rest } = useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodos(),\n  })\n  return { todos, ...rest }\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"correct"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const todosQuery = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: () => api.getTodos(),\n})\n\n// normal object destructuring is fine\nconst { data: todos } = todosQuery","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"link","href":"https://typescript-eslint.io/getting-started/typed-linting/","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typed linting"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is enabled, the rule also flags rest destructuring on custom hooks that return a TanStack Query result."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-not-to-use-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When Not To Use It"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you set the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notifyOnChangeProps"},{"type":"text","value":" options manually, you can disable this rule.\nSince you are not using tracked queries, you are responsible for specifying which props should trigger a re-render."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"attributes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attributes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ Recommended"}]}],"checked":true},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🔧 Fixable"}]}],"checked":false}]}],"headings":[{"id":"rule-details","text":"Rule Details","level":2},{"id":"when-not-to-use-it","text":"When Not To Use It","level":2},{"id":"attributes","text":"Attributes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nUse object rest destructuring on query results automatically subscribes to every field of the query result, which may cause unnecessary re-renders.\nThis makes sure that you only subscribe to the fields that you actually need.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/no-rest-destructuring\": \"warn\" */\n\nconst useTodos = () => {\n  const { data: todos, ...rest } = useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodos(),\n  })\n  return { todos, ...rest }\n}\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\nconst todosQuery = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: () => api.getTodos(),\n})\n\n// normal object destructuring is fine\nconst { data: todos } = todosQuery\n```\n\nWhen [typed linting](https://typescript-eslint.io/getting-started/typed-linting/) is enabled, the rule also flags rest destructuring on custom hooks that return a TanStack Query result.\n\n## When Not To Use It\n\nIf you set the `notifyOnChangeProps` options manually, you can disable this rule.\nSince you are not using tracked queries, you are responsible for specifying which props should trigger a re-render.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended\n- [ ] 🔧 Fixable\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: no-rest-destructuring\ntitle: Disallow object rest destructuring on query results\n---\n\nUse object rest destructuring on query results automatically subscribes to every field of the query result, which may cause unnecessary re-renders.\nThis makes sure that you only subscribe to the fields that you actually need.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/no-rest-destructuring\": \"warn\" */\n\nconst useTodos = () => {\n  const { data: todos, ...rest } = useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['todos'],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodos(),\n  })\n  return { todos, ...rest }\n}\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\nconst todosQuery = useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n  queryFn: () => api.getTodos(),\n})\n\n// normal object destructuring is fine\nconst { data: todos } = todosQuery\n```\n\nWhen [typed linting](https://typescript-eslint.io/getting-started/typed-linting/) is enabled, the rule also flags rest destructuring on custom hooks that return a TanStack Query result.\n\n## When Not To Use It\n\nIf you set the `notifyOnChangeProps` options manually, you can disable this rule.\nSince you are not using tracked queries, you are responsible for specifying which props should trigger a re-render.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended\n- [ ] 🔧 Fixable\n"}
